# Local-only inference (no cloud APIs)

Do not call cloud model, search, storage, or upload APIs for this workspace. That includes DashScope, OpenRouter, OrcaRouter, Cheaper Inference, MiniMax, Serper/Tavily/Exa/Serply, `WebSearch`, `WebFetch`, `GenerateImage`, hosted `qwen-mm-plugins-api` (vision_chat, OCR, grounding, Omni, `transcribe_audio` without a local server), and any other remote endpoint that would receive local files or conversation content.

Keep `QWEN_MM_NATIVE_MODE=1`. Core MCP (`read_image`, `read_video`, `visualize`, `media_info`, crop/draw) may run locally. Do not use caption fallback (`NATIVE_MODE=0`), which uploads images.

## Visual tasks

Use the local Unsloth OpenAI-compatible server (do not send pixels to a hosted VL API):

```bash
unsloth run \
  --model unsloth/Qwen3-VL-2B-Instruct-GGUF:UD-Q2_K_XL \
  --disable-tools \
  --reasoning off \
  --api-only \
  -H 127.0.0.1 \
  -p 8888
```

Bind **127.0.0.1** only. `-H 0.0.0.0` makes Unsloth report the port as reachable from the public internet. `--api-only` keeps the Studio UI from unloading this GGUF.

Client: `http://127.0.0.1:8888/v1` (`/v1/chat/completions`). Model id: `unsloth/Qwen3-VL-2B-Instruct-GGUF`. Quant: `Qwen3-VL-2B-Instruct-UD-Q2_K_XL.gguf`. `--disable-tools` must stay on so the server cannot web-search. Auth: local `DASHSCOPE_API_KEY` in `~/.qwen-mm-plugins/config` (Unsloth `sk-unsloth-…` key, never a cloud key).

## Audio tasks

Use local Unsloth `unsloth/Qwen3-0.6B-GGUF` 4-bit (default port **8889** so it does not collide with vision):

```bash
unsloth run \
  --model unsloth/Qwen3-0.6B-GGUF:UD-Q4_K_XL \
  --disable-tools \
  --reasoning off \
  -H 127.0.0.1 \
  -p 8889
```

Client: `http://127.0.0.1:8889/v1`. Do not use DashScope ASR. If a server is down, start the matching `unsloth run` command locally; do not fail over to a hosted API.
